&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Below is the annual On Target Compensation (OTE) range for candidates located in Germany. Your actual OTE, which is inclusive of base salary and incentive compensation, will depend on factors such as your skills, qualifications, experience, and work location. In addition, Okta offers equity (where applicable) and comprehensive financial benefits including paid time off and parental leave in accordance with our applicable plans and policies. To learn more about our Total Rewards program please visit: https://rewards.okta.com/deu.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The OTE range for this position for candidates located in Germany is between:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€196.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€270.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Who we are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Typeform is a refreshingly different form builder. We help over 150,000 businesses collect the data they need with forms, surveys, and quizzes that people enjoy. Designed to look striking and feel effortless to fill out, Typeform drives 500 million responses every year—and integrates with essential tools like Slack, Zapier, and Hubspot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Typeform&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Typeform helps people create better conversations at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Millions of people use Typeform to collect information, understand their customers, generate leads, run research, gather feedback, and power workflows across their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are continuing to evolve Typeform from a form builder into a broader platform for collecting, understanding, and acting on information. AI is becoming a major part of that direction, both through experiences we build for customers and through making Typeform easier for AI agents and other products to interact with.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Product Manager to help shape what comes next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager at Typeform, you will own a meaningful product area and work closely with Engineering, Design, Data, Research, Marketing, and other teams to turn customer problems and business opportunities into products people genuinely want to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for understanding the problem space, setting product direction, deciding where the team should focus, and helping the team move from insight to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a role where Product simply writes requirements and hands them to Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect our Product Managers to be close to customers, opinionated about the problems worth solving, comfortable making decisions with incomplete information, and able to bring teams together around a clear direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will balance customer value, product quality, technical considerations, and commercial impact while helping the team move quickly and learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and roadmap for a key area of the Typeform product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong understanding of our customers, their workflows, and the problems they are trying to solve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities through customer conversations, behavioural data, research, market insight, and product intuition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn broad problems into clear product bets, hypotheses, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Design and Engineering from discovery through delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Data and Research to understand customer behaviour and evaluate whether what we build is working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful prioritisation decisions across customer needs, business goals, technical investment, and product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success measures and use them to guide product decisions before and after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run experiments where appropriate and use the results to shape future product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, and other teams to ensure we understand the wider customer and commercial context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product direction clearly and build alignment across teams and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams move from ideas to shipped experiences without losing sight of the original customer problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look beyond individual features and think about how your product area contributes to the wider Typeform platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore how AI can improve the customer experience, change existing workflows, and create new ways for customers to get value from Typeform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have significant experience building and scaling digital products, ideally within SaaS, product led growth, collaboration software, productivity tools, or another strong product environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable taking on messy, ambiguous product problems and bringing structure and direction to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong focus on customer problems and outcomes, rather than jumping straight to features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgement, with the ability to use customer insight, data, and context to make good decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close collaboration with Engineering and Design, with product development treated as a shared discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to set a clear product direction while staying practical about what the team should focus on next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident making trade offs, making decisions, and explaining the thinking behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good judgement around when to experiment, when to research, and when there is enough evidence to move forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication, with the ability to adapt complex ideas for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial awareness and an understanding of how product decisions can influence activation, engagement, retention, expansion, and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about AI and how it is changing the way products are built and how customers interact with software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A real care for product quality and the details that shape a strong customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You might be particularly strong in one or more of these areas&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We do not expect every Senior Product Manager to have the same background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depending on the team, relevant experience could include:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product led growth, onboarding, activation, or retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creation tools, editors, builders, or content creation experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform products, APIs, integrations, or developer ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytics, insights, research, or data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pricing, packaging, payments, or monetisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI powered products, agents, automation, or intelligent workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2B SaaS products used across multiple teams and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Typeform drives hundreds of millions of interactions each year, enabling conversational, human-centered experiences across the globe. We &lt;strong&gt;move as one team&lt;/strong&gt;, empowering our collective efforts by valuing each individual’s unique perspective. This fosters &lt;strong&gt;strong bonds&lt;/strong&gt; grounded in respect, transparency, and trust. We &lt;strong&gt;champion our diverse customer base&lt;/strong&gt; by anticipating their needs and addressing their challenges with priority. Committed to excellence, we&lt;strong&gt; hold high expectations &lt;/strong&gt;for ourselves and each other, continuously striving to deliver exceptional results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and stand firmly against discrimination and harassment of any kind—whether based on race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or expression, or veteran status. Everyone is welcome here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The world of digital assets is accelerating in speed, magnitude, and complexity, opening the door to new ways for leveraging the blockchain. Fireblocks’ platform and network provide the simplest and most secure way for companies to work with digital assets and it trusted by some of the largest financial institutions, banks, globally-recognized brands, and Web3 companies in the world, including BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Revolut, and thousands more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Fireblocks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;Fireblocks is the institutional standard for digital asset security and settlement. We enable banks, fintechs, and exchanges—like BNY Mellon, Revolut, and ANZ—to securely navigate the blockchain economy. Our platform and network provide the simplest and most secure way for companies to work with digital assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Mission: Quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;The Financial Apps unit builds the critical infrastructure that connects institutions to the digital asset economy. Our products cover everything from staking and yield to on-ramps, exchange integrations, and Web3 connectivity (e.g. WalletConnect).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll manually test all flows that need validation, and contribute to building out our automation the rest of the time. We need someone who treats quality as a holistic product challenge, takes pride in rigorous manual testing, and is eager to help grow our automation—using AI to move faster at every stage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Quality Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; You own the quality of the product end-to-end. You don&#39;t just test against a spec; you analyze the spec, find the logical gaps, and suggest improvements to ensure a better final product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On Manual QA:&lt;/strong&gt; You design and execute thorough manual test plans across complex financial and Web3 flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Powered Velocity:&lt;/strong&gt; You leverage AI agents (e.g., Claude Code) to accelerate your workflow, expand coverage, and ship faster without sacrificing depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep-Dive Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; You are comfortable digging into logs and monitoring tools (Datadog/Sentry) to understand why something broke. You aren&#39;t afraid to get your hands dirty in the backend to find the root cause.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; When you&#39;re not running manual flows, you help build and maintain automation across backend APIs and frontend interfaces in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; You don&#39;t see yourself as &quot;just a tester.&quot; You are an engineer with a product mindset who actively works to improve the systems you are checking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You take real pride in finding what others miss — exploratory testing and edge-case hunting genuinely excite you, and you&#39;d rather break something today than let a user break it tomorrow. You do both automation and manual testing, and treat both as core parts of the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;3+ years in Manual QA&amp;nbsp;with hands-on automation experience across the full stack (TypeScript preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Solid grasp of blockchain fundamentals, the transaction lifecycle, and DeFi logic like staking and bridging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;AI-native - you already use AI tools daily to move faster and cut through complex errors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Fast learner - new domains don&#39;t slow you down; you keep pace in an industry that moves at the speed of crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Data-driven debugger - when something breaks, logs are your first move, not your last resort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Please see our candidate privacy policy here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some key info for you about Liberis:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌱 We were founded in 2007&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 We have provided over $3bn of funding to small businesses so far&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 We have been named in&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CNBC &amp;amp; Statista Top 150 UK Fintechs for 2025&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍 We&#39;re a global team, with a dynamic presence in&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;key locations around the world&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧠 We&#39;re a thriving community of over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;290&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;innovative minds&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👩🏾 🤝 👨🏼 We&#39;re a vibrant melting pot, celebrating over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;27&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;nationalities in our team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏢 Our team brings experience from over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;740&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;previous companies, from startups to global giants&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎯 We have just been named as one of&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech’s Finest 50&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;by Welcome to the Jungle&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪 We’re proud to be an accredited&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real Living Wage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;employer, ensuring everyone is paid fairly for the great work they do!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Product &amp;amp; Engineering Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liberis is building the embedded finance platform that lets partners around the world offer innovative funding products to their small business customers. We&#39;re a growth-stage fintech with teams in London, Nottingham, Atlanta, Stockholm, Munich and Mumbai, and we’re building a global Product, Data &amp;amp; Engineering team that thrives on autonomy, ownership, and is focused on impact! Our teams solve real-world problems for small businesses, shaping products that unlock opportunity at scale.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering is going through an AI-first transformation, rethinking how teams are structured and how they ship. It&#39;s changing what a small team can do! We empower our teams to make decisions, move fast, and take full responsibility for the solutions they deliver. You’ll join a team where curiosity is encouraged and collaboration across Product, Data, Delivery and Engineering is the norm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join Liberis’ Product Design team, working alongside product managers, engineers, and researchers across the business to help shape exceptional financial experiences to support small business!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Product Designer to help evolve the internal systems our teams rely on and the service journeys that connect them to our merchants and partners. You’ll take ownership of design problems from discovery through to shipped, polished interfaces, partnering closely with product managers and engineers along the way!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role focused primarily on design delivery within our fulfilment area. You’ll work on complex workflows and internal systems used by teams including Operations, Underwriting and Collections, turning an established product vision into well-considered features that can be shipped in manageable increments. Success in this role looks like well-crafted, research informed interfaces that ship on time!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a collaborative environment with engaged users and a strong front-end engineering team. Because the people using your work are close to the product team, you’ll have regular opportunities to understand their needs, test ideas and see the immediate impact of what you deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll get to do in the role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Liberis, our internal systems are at the core of how we support small businesses. In this role, you&#39;ll design and ship the interfaces our operational teams rely on every day, turning complex workflows into clear, usable tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with your Product Manager and Engineering Manager throughout the product lifecycle, from discovery and early concepts through to delivery and post-launch iteration, shaping decisions together rather than handing off a finished design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll build and iterate on high-fidelity UI in Figma, taking designs from early wireframes through to pixel-perfect, developer-ready screens, and take ownership of our design system, keeping components and patterns consistent across the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work directly with the operational teams who use these systems day to day, running interviews and usability testing to understand where the friction is, and mapping their end-to-end journeys to find where processes break down and spot opportunities to fix them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we think you’ll need:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable facilitating UX research and communicating findings clearly to validate your decisions for new product features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think strategically about the long-term implications of design decisions and are used to planning well beyond the feature immediately required to ensure products continue to evolve with clear direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Figma experience is essential for this role, including knowledge of component best practice, auto layout and variant management. Experience using developer handover features would also be highly beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your design process is highly collaborative; you iterate openly and validate quickly with feedback from stakeholders and design peers before aligning on a path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working alongside engineers to turn designs into shipped product features, with an awareness of feasibility and technical dependencies. You judge your work by what’s shipped, not what’s in your design file.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prototype at pace with a high level of interactivity and attention to detail to bring designs to life for stakeholders and users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running usability testing and validating that products meet user expectations and adhere to WCAG accessibility standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of service design strategies including service blueprints, user journey maps and identifying opportunities across multi-channel processes.
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
