&lt;p&gt;London&lt;br&gt;4 days/week in office&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;9 Month Fixed-Term Contract&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are you a senior analyst who thinks strategically about data and can influence how an organisation uses it to make decisions?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are you someone who can step into an established portfolio of work at pace and set the bar for how we manage data quality, governance and insight?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you&#39;ve operated at Principal or Lead Analyst level in fintech or a regulated, data-heavy industry, and you&#39;re energised by moving between hands-on analysis to acting as a strategic partner to the business, this could be the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modulr is the payments automation platform that streamlines money movement with accuracy, control and reliability – built to scale. We process more than 200m transactions and over £180bn in payment value on an annualised basis, and we&#39;re trusted by over 6,000 businesses from fast-growing SMEs to global enterprises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We automate how money moves into and out of a business – payroll, supplier payments, spend management and payment collection – through a single platform, connected to the accounting and payroll systems finance teams already use and underpinned by principal memberships of Visa and Mastercard and direct access to central bank infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a regulated payments provider with over a decade of experience, we&#39;re the platform finance teams trust to run mission-critical operations. Modulr is backed by PayPal, FIS, General Atlantic, Blenheim Chalcot, Frog Capital and Highland Europe, with over 400 employees across London, Edinburgh, Amsterdam and Mumbai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about us on our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.modulrfinance.com/&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.modulrfinance.com/life-at-modulr&quot;&gt;careers site&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Analysis &amp;amp; Strategic Insight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the synthesis of complex, multi-source data to drive organisation-wide insight and shape high-level strategic decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Leadership &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted voice and influencer across the business, engaging stakeholders directly to shape organisational data strategy and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Governance &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic oversight of data management across Modulr, define governance standards and policy, and contribute to the long-term data strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and champion organisational standards for data modelling, quality assurance, validation, and enrichment — and develop best practice frameworks that others follow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Visualisation &amp;amp; Insight Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the standard for how we visualise and communicate data insights, leading the strategic direction of the practice across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Mentoring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop analysts on the team, building capability and raising the quality of analytical work during a period of leadership transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience operating at Principal, Lead or Senior Analyst level, ideally within fintech, payments or another regulated, data-intensive industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of translating complex data into insight that genuinely shapes data-driven decisions across an organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in data modelling, quality assurance and visualisation, with the confidence and judgement to set standards rather than just follow them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong statistical and analytical grounding — you&#39;re comfortable moving between hands-on analysis and strategic oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to step into an established team and portfolio of work at short notice, with the confidence to keep initiatives moving without an extended ramp-up period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring and developing analytical teams, especially during periods of transition or change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to high-stakes, high-visibility data challenges in a fast-growing, regulated fintech or financial services business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModInclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Modulr, we are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team and fostering a culture where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences and perspectives. If you need any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
